.TH ldns-compare-zones-rrr 1 "27 Oct 2026"
.SH NAME
ldns-compare-zones-rrr \- compare two snapshots of a zone RRset by RRset
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ldns-compare-zones-rrr
.IR [-s]
.IR [-h]
.IR [-v]
.IR ZONEFILE1
.IR ZONEFILE2
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBldns-compare-zones-rrr\fR reads two snapshots of the same DNS zone, where
ZONEFILE2 is the later one (its SOA serial must not be lower than that of
ZONEFILE1). Both zones are walked RRset by RRset, each RRset together with the
RRSIGs covering it, and the difference between the two SOA serial numbers is
printed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-s\fR
Do not sort the zones.
.TP
\fB-h\fR
Show usage and exit
.TP
\fB-v\fR
Show the version and exit
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Triet Huynh, based on ldns-compare-zones.
